@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# KV Cache Manager TTNN Operations
+
+This directory is the TTNN build-time integration layer used by the external
+`kvcache-manager` package. It owns device operations, the wire ABI, and device
+kernels that must be built with the matching tt-metal revision.
+
+It does not own the product `Client` or `Server` lifecycle. TTNN does not export
+C++ façade classes or Python `ttnn.kvcache_manager.Client` and
+`ttnn.kvcache_manager.Server` objects. Product lifecycle, session establishment,
+connection management, host backing, tiering, policy, and the persistent
+server host runtime are built by the `kvcache-manager` repository.
+
+## Source boundary
+
+TTNN retains:
+
+- `client/client.cpp` and `client/client_operations.hpp`: the opaque operation
+  runtime used to build and enqueue PING, PUT, GET, EXISTS, REMOVE, MOVE,
+  FLUSH, and related client-side device programs, including the resident
+  multi-client GET workload used by product `Client.get_parallel`;
+- `client/device/kernels`: client request and transfer kernels;
+- `server/device/kernels`: persistent server device kernels;
+- `gather`: TTNN gather, scatter, pack, and unpack operations;
+- `common/protocol`: host/device wire structs and memory layout;
+- `common/config.*`, Fabric helpers, bootstrap protocol, and descriptor wire types.
+
+The `ClientOperations` type is an internal operation boundary, not the product
+Client façade. Its factory returns an opaque handle so the external manager can
+issue operations without compiling TTNN operation sources itself.
+
+TTNN must not contain or compile:
+
+- a public KV cache `Client` or `Server` façade;
+- Client connection, session lifecycle, or quarantine orchestration;
+- Server lifecycle, host backing, tiering, or host policy;
+- manager-owned native bindings or Python lifecycle wrappers.
+
+## Python API
+
+`ttnn.kvcache_manager` exposes only TTNN operations and constants:
+
+- `MAX_CLIENTS`
+- `gather_tp_shards_to_chip`
+- `scatter_chunk_from_chip`
+- `pack_local_shards`
+- `unpack_local_shards`
+- `reserve_gather_resources`
+- `release_gather_resources`
+
+Applications import `Client` and `Server` from the separately built
+`kvcache_manager` package.
+
+Static cross-node deployments may select a Server worker group and cable lane
+through the opaque operation configuration. With eight Server shards and two
+links, the manager runtime builds two lane-local MUXes and places all persistent
+Server producers in the same workload; TTNN supplies the matching device sender
+implementation but still owns no Server lifecycle object.
+
+## Build and installation
+
+The component is part of the normal TTNN build. The installed development
+surface consists only of the operation ABI and wire/configuration headers
+listed by this directory's `CMakeLists.txt`. Device kernel sources are installed
+as TTNN runtime assets because Metal programs compile them at runtime.
+
+`kvcache-manager` must build against an installed TTNN package from the exact
+matching tt-metal revision. It must not inject its sources into the TTNN build,
+and TTNN must not require the manager repository.
+
+## Validation
+
+Host-side protocol, configuration, descriptor, and operation ABI checks live in
+`tests/ttnn/unit_tests/gtests/test_kvcache_manager_config.cpp`; the static return-route encoding is
+pinned by `test_kvcache_manager_return_route.cpp`.
+Product lifecycle and device smoke tests belong to `kvcache-manager`.
+
+The authoritative numeric wire and memory layouts are
+`common/protocol/packet.hpp` and `common/protocol/layout.hpp`. See
+[`docs/design.md`](docs/design.md) for the device-operation invariants. Prose
+must not duplicate numeric offsets from those headers.
